license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: "A reconciliation proves the books against an outside record, usually a bank statement: the opening balance plus every transaction has to equal the printed closing balance, and any difference has to be explained by a specific item, such as a check not yet cashed. Each folder here works through one kind of reconciliation with a small fictional data file that adds up exactly."
keywords:
  - bank-reconciliation
  - reconciliation
  - proof-of-cash
  - bookkeeping
  - accounting
  - small-business
  - csv
date-released: 2026-10-15
